//  Shared thinking-spinner sheet. Seventeen 16x16 cells.
//
//  spin.1 .. spin.8       the ring, highlight travelling clockwise
//  spinflip.1 .. .8       the same frames MIRRORED
//  blank                  deliberately empty
//
//  WHY A MIRRORED SET EXISTS
//
//  The engine mirrors a monster's whole animation with facing direction, and
//  mirroring a rotation reverses it -- a spinner that runs clockwise facing
//  right runs anticlockwise facing left. Handing the engine pre-mirrored art
//  when the unit faces left cancels that out exactly. This needs nothing of the
//  artwork: it does NOT have to be symmetric about the vertical axis, which the
//  ring is not (the dot positions round to the pixel grid unevenly).
//
//  The alternative is a transformation group scaled by -1 on x. That is one
//  call and keeps the animation's phase through a turn, where switching states
//  restarts the cycle. Use this set only if transformation groups turn out not
//  to work on a monster animator.
//
//  <frame> is 1-indexed in .animation files, so a "frames" : 8 state expands to
//  spin.1 .. spin.8. Do not renumber from zero.

{
  "frameGrid" : {
    "size" : [16, 16],
    "dimensions" : [17, 1],
    "names" : [
      [ "spin.1", "spin.2", "spin.3", "spin.4",
        "spin.5", "spin.6", "spin.7", "spin.8",
        "spinflip.1", "spinflip.2", "spinflip.3", "spinflip.4",
        "spinflip.5", "spinflip.6", "spinflip.7", "spinflip.8",
        "blank" ]
    ]
  }
}
